<li>The Status buffer</li>
<li>The <kbd>?</kbd> key to get help</li>
<li>Staging hunks instead of the whole file</li>
<li>The various type of commits</li>
<li>The log functions</li>
<li>Blame</li>
<li>Stashing</li>
<li>Interactive rebasing</li>
<li>Resolving merge conflicts</li>
<li>The Forge interface</li>
</ol>
<p>
At the end, he has a very nice cheat sheet that breaks out the commands by subsystem.
</p>
<p>
This is a really nice post that should be useful even if you are already familiar with Magit and Git. Give it look.</p>
